s price line drawn through a label passes check.py, although the layout code clears grid lines and GENERATOR item 3 says no drawn line strikes a label", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. The probe selects only 'line.axis, line.floor' (docs/eval-report-kit/scripts/check.py:48). kVLine (kit.js:144) and _vline (chart_svg.py:442) also cut grid lines around the chart's head, a reference label and the group headings. GENERATOR.md section 8 item 3 states the general rule ('no drawn line strikes a label through'), while its lead and item 3's parenthesis correctly limit the automated part to axes and reference lines. A regression in the grid's clear boxes, or a scatter's price_line, which no clear set covers, would ship with check.py and test_presentation_chart_clearance.py passing. A hairline grid may be excluded on purpose. If so, nothing is owed. If not, add 'line.grid' to the probe's selector.", "files": ["docs/eval-report-kit/scripts/check.py", "docs/eval-report-kit/GENERATOR.md"], "fid": "R-19"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "severity": "note", "title": "Shipped source narrates review history: html_parts.py cites \"Discodon's C5b re-shoot\", and kit.js and chart_svg.py record what the interval read at its former .35 opacity", "recommendation": "Scope: class. Search packages/evals/src and docs/eval-report-kit/kit for 're-shoot', 'C5' and 'at .35'. It broke because the incident that motivated a rule was written into the rule's comment. html_parts.py:783 names a work-cycle ('C5b re-shoot'), which resolves nowhere in the repo. kit.js:217 and chart_svg.py:1151 say 'at .35 opacity it read 1.6:1 in light and 1.5:1 in dark', which describes a drawing that no longer exists. Delete the history clauses and keep the rule itself (an interval at full strength reads at the 3:1 that WCAG 1.4.11 asks of a mark). Nothing reads these comments, so no other edit is wanted. Test docstrings citing 5757aa3ae are left alone, since a commit hash resolves.", "files": ["packages/eva